# Root-level safety net. Each service also has its own .gitignore
# (backend/, frontend/, ai-service/) — git applies those too. The rules
# here are duplicated on purpose: if a service's .gitignore is ever
# edited or a new service is added, secrets and build output still stay
# out of version control.

# Secrets — never commit. .env.example files ARE tracked (see below).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies
node_modules/
venv/
.venv/

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Prisma's generated client — platform-specific binaries (~15MB).
# Regenerated by `npx prisma generate` during install/deploy.
generated/prisma/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.pem
.idea/
.vscode/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Deployment
.vercel

# AI assistant instructions — local to each dev's setup, not project source
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Per-developer tool settings. .claude/launch.json IS tracked — it
# documents how to start the three services.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Personal interview prep notes — private, never publish.
# The real copy lives OUTSIDE this repo; this is a safety net in case a
# copy is ever dropped in here. Matches the exact filename only, so it
# cannot catch src/components/applications/interview-prep-card.tsx.
interview-prep.md
/interview-prep*.md

# docs/WALKTHROUGH.md is the same kind of thing under a neutral name: it
# is written to be read before an interview, and §5 is a list of this
# codebase's weak spots. Kept on disk, untracked. It was tracked until
# Aug 2026, so it is still readable in this repo's history — see the note
# in the commit that removed it.
/docs/WALKTHROUGH.md
